('gd-opening', 'Group discussion opening', 'gd', 'Write a 60-90 word opening statement for the GD topic: "Is remote work better than working from the office?"', 'Define the topic, take a balanced or clear stance, and give one or two reasons with an example. Invite discussion.', 'Remote work became mainstream after 2020, and the question today is not whether it works, but where it works best. Remote work saves commuting time and widens the talent pool — many companies reported stable productivity. However, office work helps new employees learn faster through informal mentoring and builds team culture. I believe a hybrid model offers the best of both: focused work at home and collaboration in the office. I would like to hear how others see its impact on freshers.', '["remote","office","however|but|on the other hand","example|for example|reported|studies","hybrid|balance|believe"]'::jsonb, 55),
('presentation-opening', 'Presentation opening', 'presentation', 'Write the first 45 seconds of a presentation introducing your final-year project to a panel (60-90 words).', 'Hook the audience with the problem, state what you built and preview the structure of your talk.', 'Good morning, everyone. Every placement season, students in our college spend hours switching between five different websites to prepare — and nobody tracks whether they are actually improving. Our project, BrainBridge, brings aptitude, coding, communication and interview practice into one platform with a personalised roadmap and daily progress tracking. In the next ten minutes, I will explain the problem, demonstrate the platform, walk you through our architecture and share the results from our pilot with forty students.', '["good morning|hello","problem","project|built|platform","demonstrate|demo|show","architecture|results|next"]'::jsonb, 55),
('handling-unknown-question', 'Handling a question you cannot answer', 'confidence', 'The interviewer asks about a technology you have not used (e.g. Kafka). Write how you would respond honestly and positively (50-80 words).', 'Be honest, relate it to what you do know, show how you would learn it, and keep a positive tone.', 'I haven''t worked with Kafka directly yet, so I don''t want to claim experience I don''t have. From what I understand, it is a distributed messaging system used for event streaming between services. In my project I used a simple job queue for sending emails asynchronously, so I understand why decoupling producers and consumers is useful. If this role uses Kafka, I would start with the official documentation and build a small producer-consumer demo to learn it quickly.', '["honest|haven''t|have not|not used","understand|know","project|used","learn|learning|documentation"]'::jsonb, 45);
