('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If LAMP is coded as MZNO, how is SALT coded?', '["RZKS","TBMU","SMZT","TZMS"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Letters in odd positions move +1, letters in even positions move -1. SALT → TZMS.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If JUMP = 60 (A = 1, B = 2, ...), what is SALT?', '["42","26","52","67"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Add the alphabet positions: S=19, A=1, L=12, T=20 → 52.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If DOG is coded as ENH, how is JUMP coded?', '["ONTK","KTNO","ITLO","KVNQ"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Letters in odd positions move +1, letters in even positions move -1. JUMP → KTNO.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If SHIP = 52 (A = 1, B = 2, ...), what is MIND?', '["40","44","32","20"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Add the alphabet positions: M=13, I=9, N=14, D=4 → 40.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If DOG is coded as ENH, how is MIND coded?', '["NHOC","LJME","NJOE","COHN"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Letters in odd positions move +1, letters in even positions move -1. MIND → NHOC.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If BOOK = 43 (A = 1, B = 2, ...), what is COLD?', '["37","28","34","40"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Add the alphabet positions: C=3, O=15, L=12, D=4 → 34.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If FISH is coded as GHTG, how is FARM coded?', '["EZQL","GZSL","LSZG","EBQN"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Letters in odd positions move +1, letters in even positions move -1. FARM → GZSL.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If FARM = 38 (A = 1, B = 2, ...), what is WORK?', '["33.5","134","67","81"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Add the alphabet positions: W=23, O=15, R=18, K=11 → 67.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If NEST is coded as OGVX, how is TREE coded?', '["IHTU","UTHI","TSGH","VTGG"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The 1st letter moves +1, 2nd +2, 3rd +3, and so on. TREE → UTHI.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If FARM is coded as 12-2-36-26, what is the code for TREE?', '["10-10-36-40","60-54-15-15","41-37-11-11","40-36-10-10"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Each letter''s position is doubled: T(20)→40, R(18)→36, E(5)→10, E(5)→10.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'In a code language, WIND is written as DRMW. How is DOG written?', '["WLT","BME","XMU","TLW"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Each letter is replaced by its opposite (A↔Z, B↔Y, ...): DOG → WLT.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If GAME is coded as HCPI, how is TREE coded?', '["VTGG","IHTU","USFF","UTHI"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The 1st letter moves +1, 2nd +2, 3rd +3, and so on. TREE → UTHI.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If JUMP is coded as 20-42-26-32, what is the code for BOOK?', '["5-31-31-23","4-30-30-22","6-45-45-33","22-30-30-4"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Each letter''s position is doubled: B(2)→4, O(15)→30, O(15)→30, K(11)→22.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'In a code language, BIRD is written as YRIW. How is DOG written?', '["BME","WLT","QBT","TLW"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Each letter is replaced by its opposite (A↔Z, B↔Y, ...): DOG → WLT.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If WORK is coded as XQUO, how is MILK coded?', '["OKNM","NKOO","NJML","MJNN"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The 1st letter moves +1, 2nd +2, 3rd +3, and so on. MILK → NKOO.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If PEN is coded as 32-10-28, what is the code for GAME?', '["15-3-27-11","21-3-39-15","14-2-26-10","8-2-14-6"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Each letter''s position is doubled: G(7)→14, A(1)→2, M(13)→26, E(5)→10.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'In a code language, MILK is written as NROP. How is FISH written?', '["DGQF","SHRU","VSIT","URHS"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Each letter is replaced by its opposite (A↔Z, B↔Y, ...): FISH → URHS.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If TEAM is coded as UGDQ, how is CODE coded?', '["DQGI","CPFH","IGQD","EQFG"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The 1st letter moves +1, 2nd +2, 3rd +3, and so on. CODE → DQGI.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If BIRD is coded as 4-18-36-8, what is the code for PEN?', '["32-10-28","33-11-29","28-10-32","48-15-42"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Each letter''s position is doubled: P(16)→32, E(5)→10, N(14)→28.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'In a code language, WORK is written as DLIP. How is TEAM written?', '["RCYK","GVZN","HWAO","GRNZ"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Each letter is replaced by its opposite (A↔Z, B↔Y, ...): TEAM → GVZN.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If CAT is coded as DCW, how is LAMP coded?', '["TPCM","MCPT","NCOR","MBNQ"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The 1st letter moves +1, 2nd +2, 3rd +3, and so on. LAMP → MCPT.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If TREE is coded as 40-36-10-10, what is the code for PLAY?', '["32-24-2-50","48-36-3-75","33-25-3-51","50-2-24-32"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Each letter''s position is doubled: P(16)→32, L(12)→24, A(1)→2, Y(25)→50.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'In a code language, RAIN is written as IZRM. How is DOG written?', '["XMU","BME","QBT","WLT"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Each letter is replaced by its opposite (A↔Z, B↔Y, ...): DOG → WLT.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If PLAY is coded as QNDC, how is CAT coded?', '["CBV","DCW","ECV","WCD"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The 1st letter moves +1, 2nd +2, 3rd +3, and so on. CAT → DCW.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'If GAME is coded as 14-2-26-10, what is the code for TREE?', '["41-37-11-11","21-19-6-6","10-10-36-40","40-36-10-10"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Each letter''s position is doubled: T(20)→40, R(18)→36, E(5)→10, E(5)→10.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'coding-and-decoding', 'In a code language, TREE is written as GIVV. How is SALT written?', '["IAPH","QYJR","HZOG","FNYG"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Each letter is replaced by its opposite (A↔Z, B↔Y, ...): SALT → HZOG.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Pointing to a man, Neha says, "He is the son of my grandfather''s only son." How is the man related to Neha?', '["Brother","Uncle","Cousin","Father"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Grandfather''s only son is Neha''s father; his son is Neha''s brother.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'A is the father of B. C is the mother of A. How is C related to B?', '["Grandmother","Mother","Sister","Aunt"]'::jsonb, 0, 'C is A''s mother and A is B''s father, so C is B''s grandmother.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'P is the brother of Q. Q is the sister of R. R is the son of S. How is P related to S?', '["Daughter","Son","Brother","Nephew"]'::jsonb, 1, 'P, Q and R are siblings and children of S. P is male (brother), so P is S''s son.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Introducing a woman, Arun says, "Her mother is the only daughter of my mother." How is the woman related to Arun?', '["Cousin","Sister","Niece","Daughter"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The only daughter of Arun''s mother is Arun''s sister. The woman is his sister''s daughter, i.e. his niece.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'If X is the husband of Y, and Z is the daughter of Y, how is X related to Z?', '["Father","Uncle","Brother","Grandfather"]'::jsonb, 0, 'X is married to Y, Z is Y''s daughter, so X is Z''s father.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'M is the son of N. N is the daughter of O. O is the husband of P. How is P related to M?', '["Aunt","Grandmother","Sister","Mother"]'::jsonb, 1, 'N''s parents are O and P. P is N''s mother, so P is M''s grandmother.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'A + B means A is the mother of B; A - B means A is the brother of B; A × B means A is the father of B. What does P × Q - R mean?', '["P is the brother of R","R is the father of P","P is the uncle of R","P is the father of R"]'::jsonb, 3, 'P is the father of Q, Q is the brother of R, so P is also the father of R.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Rita''s father''s only brother''s wife is Rita''s:', '["Mother","Sister","Aunt","Grandmother"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Father''s brother is uncle; his wife is aunt.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Kiran is the son of Mohan''s father''s sister. How is Kiran related to Mohan?', '["Nephew","Cousin","Uncle","Brother"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Mohan''s father''s sister is Mohan''s aunt; her son is Mohan''s cousin.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'A is B''s sister. C is B''s mother. D is C''s father. E is D''s mother. How is A related to D?', '["Niece","Granddaughter","Daughter","Grandmother"]'::jsonb, 1, 'A is a daughter of C, and C is D''s child, so A is D''s granddaughter.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Looking at a photo, Ajay says, "Her father is the only son of my father." How is the girl in the photo related to Ajay?', '["Cousin","Niece","Daughter","Sister"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The only son of Ajay''s father is Ajay himself, so the girl is his daughter.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Pointing to a woman, Rahul says, "She is the daughter of my father''s only son." How is she related to Rahul?', '["Cousin","Daughter","Sister","Niece"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Rahul''s father''s only son is Rahul himself, so she is his daughter.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'A is the son of B. B is the brother of C. C is the mother of D. How is A related to D?', '["Uncle","Brother","Nephew","Cousin"]'::jsonb, 3, 'B and C are siblings; A is B''s son and D is C''s child → A and D are cousins.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Sunita is the wife of Rakesh. Rakesh''s sister is Priya. How is Priya related to Sunita?', '["Mother-in-law","Cousin","Sister-in-law","Sister"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Husband''s sister is sister-in-law.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'X''s mother is the sister of Y''s father. How is X related to Y?', '["Uncle/Aunt","Brother/Sister","Cousin","Nephew/Niece"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Children of siblings are cousins.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'If P is the mother of Q, Q is the sister of R, and R is the father of S, how is P related to S?', '["Aunt","Mother","Grandmother","Great-grandmother"]'::jsonb, 2, 'P is mother of Q and R (siblings). R is S''s father → P is S''s grandmother.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Pointing to a boy, Kavita says, "He is the son of the only son of my grandfather." How is the boy related to Kavita?', '["Cousin","Nephew","Brother","Son"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Only son of her grandfather = her father. His son = her brother.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'A family has a grandfather, two fathers, two sons and one grandson. What is the minimum number of people?', '["6","3","4","5"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Grandfather → father → son: grandfather is a father, the middle man is both father and son, the youngest is son and grandson. 3 people.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'A @ B means A is the brother of B; A # B means A is the mother of B; A $ B means A is the wife of B. What does P # Q @ R mean?', '["P is the wife of R","R is the mother of P","P is the mother of R","P is the sister of R"]'::jsonb, 2, 'P is Q''s mother and Q is R''s brother, so P is R''s mother too.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Amit''s father''s brother''s son is Amit''s:', '["Nephew","Brother","Uncle","Cousin"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Father''s brother = uncle; uncle''s son = cousin.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'Introducing a man, a woman says, "His wife is the only daughter of my mother." How is the man related to the woman?', '["Husband","Brother","Father","Brother-in-law"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The only daughter of her mother is the woman herself, so the man is her husband.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'blood-relations', 'D is the brother of B. M is the brother of B. K is the father of M. T is the wife of K. How is B related to T?', '["Nephew","Son or daughter","Son only","Daughter only"]'::jsonb, 1, 'B is a sibling of M, whose parents are K and T. B''s gender is not given, so B is T''s son or daughter.', 'hard'),
