('logical', 'seating-arrangements', 'Five friends A, B, C, D, E sit in a row facing north. C is in the middle. A is to the immediate left of C. E is at the right end. B is to the left of A. Who sits between C and E?', '["D","A","None","B"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Order from left: B, A, C, D, E. D sits between C and E.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', 'In a row of 5 chairs, Amit sits at one end, Bina sits next to Amit, Chetan sits in the middle and Deepa sits at the other end. Where does Esha sit?', '["Next to Amit","Between Chetan and Deepa","Between Amit and Bina","At an end"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Order: Amit, Bina, Chetan, Esha, Deepa.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', 'A, B, C, D sit around a square table facing the centre. A is opposite C. B is to the right of A. Who is to the left of A?', '["C","Cannot be determined","D","B"]'::jsonb, 2, 'On a square table, A''s neighbours are B and D. B is on A''s right, so D is on A''s left.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', 'Seven people sit in a row. G is third from the left. F is to the immediate right of G. H is at the extreme right. Only two people sit between F and H. Who sits immediately to the right of F?', '["H","Nobody","G","One of the two between F and H"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Positions: G=3, F=4, H=7, so seats 5 and 6 are between F and H; the person at seat 5 is immediately right of F.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', 'Eight friends sit around a circular table facing the centre. If each person is opposite exactly one person, how many pairs of opposite people are there?', '["4","8","6","2"]'::jsonb, 0, '8 people → 8/2 = 4 opposite pairs.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', 'P, Q, R, S, T sit in a row. R is between P and S. Q is at one end, to the left of P. T is at the right end. What is the order from left?', '["Q P R S T","P R S Q T","Q S R P T","Q R P S T"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Q at the left end, then P, R (between P and S), S, then T at the right end.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', 'In a circular arrangement of 6 people facing the centre, A is second to the left of B. C is opposite B. Who sits between A and C (taking the shorter side)?', '["B","Two people","Nobody - they are adjacent","Cannot be determined"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Number the seats with B at 0. Second to the left of B is seat 2 (left = clockwise when facing centre); opposite B is seat 3. Seats 2 and 3 are adjacent.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'puzzles', 'Four students - Asha, Bala, Chitra and Dev - like different subjects: Maths, Physics, Chemistry, Biology. Asha does not like Maths or Biology. Bala likes Physics. Dev likes Biology. What does Asha like?', '["Chemistry","Biology","Maths","Physics"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Bala = Physics, Dev = Biology. Asha cannot be Maths, so Asha = Chemistry and Chitra = Maths.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'puzzles', 'A, B, C and D have different heights. A is taller than B but shorter than C. D is shorter than B. Who is the shortest?', '["A","B","D","C"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Order: C > A > B > D.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'puzzles', 'Five boxes P, Q, R, S, T are stacked. Q is directly above S. P is at the bottom. T is directly below R. S is directly above P. Which box is at the top?', '["Q","R","T","S"]'::jsonb, 1, 'From bottom: P, S, Q. T is below R, so the stack is P, S, Q, T, R → R is on top.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'puzzles', 'Three people (X, Y, Z) work in three cities (Pune, Delhi, Chennai). X does not work in Pune. Y works in Chennai. Where does Z work?', '["Delhi","Pune","Cannot be determined","Chennai"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Y = Chennai. X cannot be Pune, so X = Delhi, leaving Pune for Z.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'puzzles', 'A lecture series runs Monday to Friday with one subject per day: DBMS, OS, CN, DSA, OOP. DSA is on Wednesday. OS is the day after DBMS. CN is on Friday. OOP is not on Monday. Which subject is on Monday?', '["OS","DSA","DBMS","OOP"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Wed = DSA, Fri = CN. OS follows DBMS, so DBMS-OS must be Mon-Tue. Thursday = OOP.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'puzzles', 'Among P, Q, R, S, T, each scored differently. P scored more than Q and R. S scored less than R but more than Q. T scored the highest. Who scored the lowest?', '["R","P","Q","S"]'::jsonb, 2, 'T > P > R > S > Q.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'puzzles', 'A clock gains 5 minutes every hour. If it is set right at 8:00 AM, what time will it show at 2:00 PM the same day?', '["2:05 PM","2:25 PM","2:35 PM","2:30 PM"]'::jsonb, 3, '6 hours × 5 minutes = 30 minutes gained → 2:30 PM.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'syllogisms', 'Statements: All cats are animals. All animals are living beings. Conclusions: I. All cats are living beings. II. Some living beings are cats.', '["Only II follows","Both I and II follow","Neither follows","Only I follows"]'::jsonb, 1, 'All cats ⊂ animals ⊂ living beings → I follows. Since cats exist within living beings, II also follows.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'syllogisms', 'Statements: Some books are pens. All pens are pencils. Conclusions: I. Some books are pencils. II. All pencils are books.', '["Neither follows","Both follow","Only I follows","Only II follows"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Books that are pens are also pencils → I follows. II is an unjustified reversal.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'syllogisms', 'Statements: No doctor is a lawyer. All lawyers are teachers. Conclusions: I. No teacher is a doctor. II. Some teachers are not doctors.', '["Both follow","Only II follows","Neither follows","Only I follows"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Teachers who are lawyers are not doctors → II follows. Other teachers may be doctors, so I does not follow.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'syllogisms', 'Statements: All engineers are graduates. Some graduates are managers. Conclusions: I. Some engineers are managers. II. Some managers are graduates.', '["Only II follows","Neither follows","Both follow","Only I follows"]'::jsonb, 0, 'II is the conversion of "Some graduates are managers". I is not certain.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'syllogisms', 'Statements: Some apples are red. Some red things are cars. Conclusions: I. Some apples are cars. II. No apple is a car.', '["Only I follows","Neither follows","Either I or II follows","Only II follows"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Neither is definite on its own, but they form a complementary pair (some / none), so either I or II is true.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'syllogisms', 'Statements: All roses are flowers. No flower is a tree. Conclusions: I. No rose is a tree. II. Some flowers are roses.', '["Only I follows","Both follow","Neither follows","Only II follows"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Roses are inside flowers, which never overlap trees → I. Roses exist in flowers → II.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'syllogisms', 'Statements: All coders are thinkers. All thinkers are readers. Conclusion: All readers are coders.', '["Follows","Partly follows","Cannot be determined","Does not follow"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Coders ⊂ thinkers ⊂ readers; the reverse is not implied.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'syllogisms', 'Statements: Some students are athletes. No athlete is lazy. Conclusions: I. Some students are not lazy. II. All students are lazy.', '["Only II follows","Only I follows","Neither follows","Both follow"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Students who are athletes are not lazy → I follows; II contradicts it.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Regular practice of aptitude tests improves speed." Conclusions: I. Practice helps in exams. II. Without practice, nobody can pass.', '["Only I follows","Only II follows","Neither follows","Both follow"]'::jsonb, 0, 'I is directly supported. II is an extreme claim not implied.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "The company has decided to hire only candidates with a CGPA of 7 or above." Conclusions: I. Candidates with CGPA 6.5 will not be hired. II. All candidates above 7 CGPA will be hired.', '["Neither follows","Only II follows","Both follow","Only I follows"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The rule excludes below-7 candidates (I), but meeting the cutoff does not guarantee hiring (II).', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Most accidents on this road happen at night." Conclusions: I. Street lighting should be improved. II. The road should be closed permanently.', '["Only I follows","Neither follows","Both follow","Only II follows"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Improving lighting is a reasonable inference; permanent closure is extreme.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Online learning platforms have grown rapidly since 2020." Conclusions: I. More people are learning online now than before 2020. II. Classroom teaching has ended.', '["Only I follows","Neither follows","Only II follows","Both follow"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Growth implies more learners (I). II is not supported.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Smoking is injurious to health" is printed on every cigarette pack. Assumptions: I. People read the warning. II. Some people may be discouraged from smoking.', '["Only II is implicit","Both are implicit","Only I is implicit","Neither is implicit"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The warning is printed assuming people read it and that it may influence some of them.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "If you want to clear the interview, prepare your projects well." Assumptions: I. Interviewers ask about projects. II. Preparation affects interview results.', '["Only II is implicit","Only I is implicit","Neither is implicit","Both are implicit"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The advice assumes projects are discussed and that preparation matters.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "All employees must complete security training by Friday." Course of action: I. Send a reminder to employees who have not completed it. II. Cancel the training.', '["Only II follows","Both follow","Only I follows","Neither follows"]'::jsonb, 2, 'A reminder supports the instruction; cancelling contradicts it.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "The new metro line has reduced travel time between the two cities by 40 minutes." Conclusions: I. The metro is faster than earlier options. II. Everyone now uses the metro.', '["Only I follows","Both follow","Only II follows","Neither follows"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Reduced travel time implies it is faster (I); usage by everyone is not stated.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Only students with 75% attendance can appear for the exam." Conclusions: I. Some students may not be allowed to appear. II. Attendance is mandatory for everyone in college.', '["Neither follows","Only II follows","Both follow","Only I follows"]'::jsonb, 3, 'I follows from the rule. II overgeneralises beyond the exam.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "The government has made helmets compulsory for two-wheeler riders." Assumptions: I. Helmets reduce injuries. II. People will follow the rule.', '["Neither is implicit","Both are implicit","Only II is implicit","Only I is implicit"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Rules are made assuming they are useful and will be followed.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Our product sales fell 20% after the competitor launched a cheaper model." Conclusions: I. Price affects buying decisions. II. The competitor''s product is of better quality.', '["Only II follows","Both follow","Only I follows","Neither follows"]'::jsonb, 2, 'I is reasonable from the timing. Quality is not mentioned.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Please do not use mobile phones inside the examination hall." Assumptions: I. Phones can be used for malpractice. II. All students carry phones.', '["Both are implicit","Only II is implicit","Neither is implicit","Only I is implicit"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The instruction assumes phones could be misused; it does not assume everyone carries one.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Many fresh graduates lack practical project experience." Courses of action: I. Colleges should include more project-based learning. II. Companies should stop hiring freshers.', '["Only I follows","Neither follows","Both follow","Only II follows"]'::jsonb, 0, 'I addresses the problem constructively; II is impractical and extreme.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "The library will remain closed on Sunday for maintenance." Conclusions: I. The library is normally open on Sundays. II. Maintenance cannot be done while the library is open.', '["Only II follows","Both follow","Neither follows","Only I follows"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Announcing a closure implies it is normally open (I). II is not necessarily true.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Learn coding to get a high-paying job" - an advertisement. Assumptions: I. People want high-paying jobs. II. Coding skills are valued by employers.', '["Only I is implicit","Neither is implicit","Both are implicit","Only II is implicit"]'::jsonb, 2, 'The advertisement relies on both ideas to be persuasive.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Despite heavy rain, the match started on time." Conclusions: I. The ground had good drainage or cover. II. Rain never affects matches.', '["Only I follows","Neither follows","Both follow","Only II follows"]'::jsonb, 0, 'I is a reasonable inference; II is an absolute claim.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Candidates must bring a printed copy of the admit card." Conclusions: I. A digital copy may not be accepted. II. The admit card is required for entry.', '["Neither follows","Only I follows","Only II follows","Both follow"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The instruction implies the card is required and specifically printed.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "The city''s air quality index crossed 300 this week." Courses of action: I. Advise people with breathing problems to stay indoors. II. Ban all vehicles permanently.', '["Only II follows","Both follow","Neither follows","Only I follows"]'::jsonb, 3, 'I is a practical short-term step; a permanent total ban is extreme.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Every employee who completes the certification will get a bonus." Conclusions: I. Ravi, who completed it, will get a bonus. II. Those without certification will be fired.', '["Only II follows","Only I follows","Neither follows","Both follow"]'::jsonb, 1, 'I applies the rule (assuming Ravi is an employee). II is unrelated.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'statement-and-conclusions', 'Statement: "Startups that focus on customer feedback grow faster." Conclusions: I. Customer feedback is useful for growth. II. Startups that ignore feedback always fail.', '["Only I follows","Both follow","Only II follows","Neither follows"]'::jsonb, 0, 'I follows; "always fail" is too strong.', 'hard'),
