('logical', 'data-sufficiency', 'What is the value of x? I. 2x + 3 = 11. II. x is a positive integer.', '["Neither is sufficient","Statement I alone is sufficient","Both together are needed","Statement II alone is sufficient"]'::jsonb, 1, 'From I, x = 4. II alone gives no value.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'data-sufficiency', 'Is N an even number? I. N is divisible by 4. II. N is divisible by 3.', '["Statement II alone is sufficient","Both together are needed","Neither is sufficient","Statement I alone is sufficient"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Divisible by 4 → even. Divisible by 3 could be odd or even.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'data-sufficiency', 'How old is Ravi? I. Ravi is 5 years older than Sita. II. Sita is 20 years old.', '["Both together are needed","Statement I alone is sufficient","Statement II alone is sufficient","Neither is sufficient"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Together: Ravi = 25. Individually neither gives his age.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'data-sufficiency', 'What is the area of the rectangle? I. Perimeter is 30 cm. II. Length is twice the breadth.', '["Neither is sufficient","Statement I alone is sufficient","Both together are needed","Statement II alone is sufficient"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Together: 2(2b + b) = 30 → b = 5, l = 10 → area 50 cm².', 'medium'),
('logical', 'data-sufficiency', 'On which day of the week was Meena born? I. Her brother was born on Tuesday. II. Meena was born two days after her brother.', '["Neither is sufficient","Statement I alone is sufficient","Statement II alone is sufficient","Both together are needed"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Together: Tuesday + 2 = Thursday.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'data-sufficiency', 'What is the speed of the train? I. It crosses a pole in 10 seconds. II. It crosses a 200 m platform in 20 seconds.', '["Statement I alone is sufficient","Both together are needed","Statement II alone is sufficient","Neither is sufficient"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Let length L and speed v: L = 10v and L + 200 = 20v → v = 20 m/s. Each alone has two unknowns.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'data-sufficiency', 'Is x > y? I. x - y = 4. II. x + y = 10.', '["Both together are needed","Statement II alone is sufficient","Statement I alone is sufficient","Neither is sufficient"]'::jsonb, 2, 'x - y = 4 > 0 directly answers the question.', 'medium'),
('logical', 'data-sufficiency', 'How many students are in the class? I. Rohan is 12th from the top and 18th from the bottom. II. There are 10 more boys than girls.', '["Statement II alone is sufficient","Statement I alone is sufficient","Neither is sufficient","Both together are needed"]'::jsonb, 1, 'From I: 12 + 18 - 1 = 29 students.', 'hard'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', '4 friends - Bala, Jay, Kavya, Nikhil - sit in a row facing north. Nikhil sits between Jay and Kavya. Nikhil sits 2th from the left. Kavya sits between Nikhil and Bala. Who sits 3th from the left?', '["Nikhil","Jay","Bala","Kavya"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Applying the clues one by one leaves exactly one arrangement (left to right): Jay, Nikhil, Kavya, Bala. So the answer is Kavya.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', '4 friends - Dev, Kavya, Lokesh, Meera - sit in a row facing north. Kavya does not sit in position 2 from the left. Dev sits somewhere to the left of Meera. Lokesh sits at the extreme left end. Kavya sits between Dev and Meera. Who sits at the extreme left end?', '["Dev","Meera","Kavya","Lokesh"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Applying the clues one by one leaves exactly one arrangement (left to right): Lokesh, Dev, Kavya, Meera. So the answer is Lokesh.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', '4 friends - Esha, Isha, Jay, Nikhil - sit in a row facing north. Jay does not sit in position 3 from the left. Nikhil sits somewhere to the left of Isha. Esha does not sit in position 3 from the left. Jay sits between Nikhil and Isha. Who sits 3th from the left?', '["Nikhil","Esha","Jay","Isha"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Applying the clues one by one leaves exactly one arrangement (left to right): Nikhil, Jay, Isha, Esha. So the answer is Isha.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', '4 friends - Asha, Gita, Jay, Meera - sit in a row facing north. Asha sits at the extreme left end. Gita sits between Jay and Meera. Jay sits immediately to the left of Gita. Who sits at the extreme right end?', '["Meera","Jay","Gita","Asha"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Applying the clues one by one leaves exactly one arrangement (left to right): Asha, Jay, Gita, Meera. So the answer is Meera.', 'easy'),
('logical', 'seating-arrangements', '4 friends - Asha, Dev, Gita, Isha - sit in a row facing north. Dev sits somewhere to the left of Asha. Dev does not sit in position 2 from the left. Asha sits between Gita and Isha. Gita sits immediately to the left of Asha. Who sits 3th from the left?', '["Gita","Asha","Isha","Dev"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Applying the clues one by one leaves exactly one arrangement (left to right): Dev, Gita, Asha, Isha. So the answer is Asha.', 'easy'),
