('Frontend Developer', 'Real-time Collaborative Whiteboard', 'advanced', 'Remote teams need to sketch together.', 'Real-time Collaborative Whiteboard is a advanced project for aspiring Frontend Developers. Remote teams need to sketch together. The goal is to build a working solution with canvas drawing and live sync, then extend it with undo/redo and export png.', '["React","Canvas API","WebSockets"]'::jsonb, '["Canvas drawing","Live sync","Undo/redo","Export PNG"]'::jsonb, 'Component-based SPA: pages → reusable components → services for API calls; state in React hooks/context; responsive CSS. For this project: React, Canvas API, WebSockets.', 'A working real-time collaborative whiteboard with: Canvas drawing; Live sync; Undo/redo; Export PNG. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["React","Canvas API","WebSockets","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a real-time collaborative whiteboard using React, Canvas API, WebSockets that supports canvas drawing, live sync, undo/redo; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Real-time Collaborative Whiteboard.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Live sync\"?","How did you structure your components?","How did you make the UI responsive and accessible?","How did you optimise performance?","How would you extend Real-time Collaborative Whiteboard if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Frontend Developer', 'Micro-frontend Shell', 'advanced', 'Large apps are split across teams.', 'Micro-frontend Shell is a advanced project for aspiring Frontend Developers. Large apps are split across teams. The goal is to build a working solution with shell app loading modules and shared design tokens, then extend it with independent deploys and routing.', '["React","Module Federation"]'::jsonb, '["Shell app loading modules","Shared design tokens","Independent deploys","Routing"]'::jsonb, 'Component-based SPA: pages → reusable components → services for API calls; state in React hooks/context; responsive CSS. For this project: React, Module Federation.', 'A working micro-frontend shell with: Shell app loading modules; Shared design tokens; Independent deploys; Routing. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["React","Module Federation","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a micro-frontend shell using React, Module Federation that supports shell app loading modules, shared design tokens, independent deploys; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Micro-frontend Shell.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Shared design tokens\"?","How did you structure your components?","How did you make the UI responsive and accessible?","How did you optimise performance?","How would you extend Micro-frontend Shell if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Notes REST API', 'beginner', 'Learn CRUD and REST design.', 'Notes REST API is a beginner project for aspiring Backend Developers. Learn CRUD and REST design. The goal is to build a working solution with crud notes and validation, then extend it with pagination and error handling.', '["Node.js","Express","PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["CRUD notes","Validation","Pagination","Error handling"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL.', 'A working notes rest api with: CRUD notes; Validation; Pagination; Error handling. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Node.js","Express","PostgreSQL","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a notes rest api using Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL that supports crud notes, validation, pagination; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Notes REST API.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Validation\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Notes REST API if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'User Authentication Service', 'beginner', 'Every app needs secure login.', 'User Authentication Service is a beginner project for aspiring Backend Developers. Every app needs secure login. The goal is to build a working solution with register/login and bcrypt hashing, then extend it with jwt and password reset flow.', '["Node.js","Express","JWT","bcrypt"]'::jsonb, '["Register/login","bcrypt hashing","JWT","Password reset flow"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Node.js, Express, JWT, bcrypt.', 'A working user authentication service with: Register/login; bcrypt hashing; JWT; Password reset flow. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Node.js","Express","JWT","bcrypt","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a user authentication service using Node.js, Express, JWT that supports register/login, bcrypt hashing, jwt; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your User Authentication Service.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"bcrypt hashing\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend User Authentication Service if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Contact Form Backend', 'beginner', 'Websites need to collect enquiries reliably.', 'Contact Form Backend is a beginner project for aspiring Backend Developers. Websites need to collect enquiries reliably. The goal is to build a working solution with validated submission and spam protection, then extend it with store in db and email notification.', '["Python","Flask","SQLite/PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["Validated submission","Spam protection","Store in DB","Email notification"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Python, Flask, SQLite/PostgreSQL.', 'A working contact form backend with: Validated submission; Spam protection; Store in DB; Email notification. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","Flask","SQLite/PostgreSQL","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a contact form backend using Python, Flask, SQLite/PostgreSQL that supports validated submission, spam protection, store in db; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Contact Form Backend.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Spam protection\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Contact Form Backend if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'File Upload Service', 'beginner', 'Apps need to accept and serve files.', 'File Upload Service is a beginner project for aspiring Backend Developers. Apps need to accept and serve files. The goal is to build a working solution with upload with size/type checks and metadata in db, then extend it with download links and delete.', '["Node.js","Multer","PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["Upload with size/type checks","Metadata in DB","Download links","Delete"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Node.js, Multer, PostgreSQL.', 'A working file upload service with: Upload with size/type checks; Metadata in DB; Download links; Delete. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Node.js","Multer","PostgreSQL","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a file upload service using Node.js, Multer, PostgreSQL that supports upload with size/type checks, metadata in db, download links; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your File Upload Service.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Metadata in DB\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend File Upload Service if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Library API', 'beginner', 'Practise relational modelling.', 'Library API is a beginner project for aspiring Backend Developers. Practise relational modelling. The goal is to build a working solution with books, authors, members and borrow/return, then extend it with joins and filters and seed data.', '["Express","PostgreSQL","SQL"]'::jsonb, '["Books, authors, members","Borrow/return","Joins and filters","Seed data"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Express, PostgreSQL, SQL.', 'A working library api with: Books, authors, members; Borrow/return; Joins and filters; Seed data. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Express","PostgreSQL","SQL","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a library api using Express, PostgreSQL, SQL that supports books, authors, members, borrow/return, joins and filters; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Library API.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Borrow/return\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Library API if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Rate-Limited Public API', 'intermediate', 'APIs must protect themselves from abuse.', 'Rate-Limited Public API is a intermediate project for aspiring Backend Developers. APIs must protect themselves from abuse. The goal is to build a working solution with api keys and token-bucket rate limiting, then extend it with usage stats and openapi docs.', '["Node.js","Redis","PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["API keys","Token-bucket rate limiting","Usage stats","OpenAPI docs"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Node.js, Redis, PostgreSQL.', 'A working rate-limited public api with: API keys; Token-bucket rate limiting; Usage stats; OpenAPI docs. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Node.js","Redis","PostgreSQL","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a rate-limited public api using Node.js, Redis, PostgreSQL that supports api keys, token-bucket rate limiting, usage stats; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Rate-Limited Public API.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Token-bucket rate limiting\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Rate-Limited Public API if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Event Booking API', 'intermediate', 'Prevent double-booking under concurrency.', 'Event Booking API is a intermediate project for aspiring Backend Developers. Prevent double-booking under concurrency. The goal is to build a working solution with seat reservation and transactions and locking, then extend it with booking expiry and tests.', '["Spring Boot / Express","PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["Seat reservation","Transactions and locking","Booking expiry","Tests"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Spring Boot / Express, PostgreSQL.', 'A working event booking api with: Seat reservation; Transactions and locking; Booking expiry; Tests. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Spring Boot / Express","PostgreSQL","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a event booking api using Spring Boot / Express, PostgreSQL that supports seat reservation, transactions and locking, booking expiry; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Event Booking API.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Transactions and locking\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Event Booking API if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Notification Service', 'intermediate', 'Apps need email/SMS/push in one place.', 'Notification Service is a intermediate project for aspiring Backend Developers. Apps need email/SMS/push in one place. The goal is to build a working solution with queue-based sending and templates, then extend it with retries and delivery status.', '["Node.js","RabbitMQ/Redis queue","PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["Queue-based sending","Templates","Retries","Delivery status"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Node.js, RabbitMQ/Redis queue, PostgreSQL.', 'A working notification service with: Queue-based sending; Templates; Retries; Delivery status. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Node.js","RabbitMQ/Redis queue","PostgreSQL","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a notification service using Node.js, RabbitMQ/Redis queue, PostgreSQL that supports queue-based sending, templates, retries; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Notification Service.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Templates\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Notification Service if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'GraphQL Course API', 'intermediate', 'Compare GraphQL with REST.', 'GraphQL Course API is a intermediate project for aspiring Backend Developers. Compare GraphQL with REST. The goal is to build a working solution with schema and resolvers and nested queries, then extend it with auth and dataloader batching.', '["Node.js","GraphQL","PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["Schema and resolvers","Nested queries","Auth","DataLoader batching"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Node.js, GraphQL, PostgreSQL.', 'A working graphql course api with: Schema and resolvers; Nested queries; Auth; DataLoader batching. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Node.js","GraphQL","PostgreSQL","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a graphql course api using Node.js, GraphQL, PostgreSQL that supports schema and resolvers, nested queries, auth; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your GraphQL Course API.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Nested queries\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend GraphQL Course API if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Search Service', 'intermediate', 'Users expect fast full-text search.', 'Search Service is a intermediate project for aspiring Backend Developers. Users expect fast full-text search. The goal is to build a working solution with full-text indexes and ranking, then extend it with filters and autocomplete.', '["PostgreSQL full-text search","Express"]'::jsonb, '["Full-text indexes","Ranking","Filters","Autocomplete"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: PostgreSQL full-text search, Express.', 'A working search service with: Full-text indexes; Ranking; Filters; Autocomplete. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["PostgreSQL full-text search","Express","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a search service using PostgreSQL full-text search, Express that supports full-text indexes, ranking, filters; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Search Service.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Ranking\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Search Service if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Payment Ledger', 'advanced', 'Money movement must be correct and auditable.', 'Payment Ledger is a advanced project for aspiring Backend Developers. Money movement must be correct and auditable. The goal is to build a working solution with double-entry ledger and idempotency keys, then extend it with reconciliation report and audit log.', '["Java/Node.js","PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["Double-entry ledger","Idempotency keys","Reconciliation report","Audit log"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Java/Node.js, PostgreSQL.', 'A working payment ledger with: Double-entry ledger; Idempotency keys; Reconciliation report; Audit log. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Java/Node.js","PostgreSQL","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a payment ledger using Java/Node.js, PostgreSQL that supports double-entry ledger, idempotency keys, reconciliation report; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Payment Ledger.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Idempotency keys\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Payment Ledger if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Microservices Order System', 'advanced', 'Understand service boundaries.', 'Microservices Order System is a advanced project for aspiring Backend Developers. Understand service boundaries. The goal is to build a working solution with order, inventory, payment services and event-driven updates, then extend it with api gateway and docker compose.', '["Node.js/Spring","Kafka/RabbitMQ","Docker"]'::jsonb, '["Order, inventory, payment services","Event-driven updates","API gateway","Docker Compose"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Node.js/Spring, Kafka/RabbitMQ, Docker.', 'A working microservices order system with: Order, inventory, payment services; Event-driven updates; API gateway; Docker Compose. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Node.js/Spring","Kafka/RabbitMQ","Docker","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a microservices order system using Node.js/Spring, Kafka/RabbitMQ, Docker that supports order, inventory, payment services, event-driven updates, api gateway; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Microservices Order System.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Event-driven updates\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Microservices Order System if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Distributed Cache Layer', 'advanced', 'Reduce database load for hot reads.', 'Distributed Cache Layer is a advanced project for aspiring Backend Developers. Reduce database load for hot reads. The goal is to build a working solution with cache-aside pattern and ttl and invalidation, then extend it with metrics and load test.', '["Redis","Node.js","k6"]'::jsonb, '["Cache-aside pattern","TTL and invalidation","Metrics","Load test"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Redis, Node.js, k6.', 'A working distributed cache layer with: Cache-aside pattern; TTL and invalidation; Metrics; Load test. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Redis","Node.js","k6","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a distributed cache layer using Redis, Node.js, k6 that supports cache-aside pattern, ttl and invalidation, metrics; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Distributed Cache Layer.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"TTL and invalidation\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Distributed Cache Layer if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Log Aggregation Pipeline', 'advanced', 'Debugging needs centralised logs.', 'Log Aggregation Pipeline is a advanced project for aspiring Backend Developers. Debugging needs centralised logs. The goal is to build a working solution with collect logs from services and parse and index, then extend it with search ui and alerts.', '["Python/Node.js","Elasticsearch/OpenSearch"]'::jsonb, '["Collect logs from services","Parse and index","Search UI","Alerts"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Python/Node.js, Elasticsearch/OpenSearch.', 'A working log aggregation pipeline with: Collect logs from services; Parse and index; Search UI; Alerts. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python/Node.js","Elasticsearch/OpenSearch","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a log aggregation pipeline using Python/Node.js, Elasticsearch/OpenSearch that supports collect logs from services, parse and index, search ui; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Log Aggregation Pipeline.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Parse and index\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Log Aggregation Pipeline if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Backend Developer', 'Multi-tenant API with RBAC', 'advanced', 'B2B apps need roles per organisation.', 'Multi-tenant API with RBAC is a advanced project for aspiring Backend Developers. B2B apps need roles per organisation. The goal is to build a working solution with organisations, roles, permissions and policy checks, then extend it with audit trail and integration tests.', '["Express/Spring","PostgreSQL"]'::jsonb, '["Organisations, roles, permissions","Policy checks","Audit trail","Integration tests"]'::jsonb, 'REST API service: routes → controllers → services → data access; relational database with migrations; auth middleware; logging and tests. For this project: Express/Spring, PostgreSQL.', 'A working multi-tenant api with rbac with: Organisations, roles, permissions; Policy checks; Audit trail; Integration tests. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Express/Spring","PostgreSQL","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a multi-tenant api with rbac using Express/Spring, PostgreSQL that supports organisations, roles, permissions, policy checks, audit trail; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Multi-tenant API with RBAC.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Policy checks\"?","How did you design your API endpoints?","How did you secure the API?","How would you scale the backend?","How would you extend Multi-tenant API with RBAC if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO project_ideas (role, title, difficulty, problem_statement, description, tech_stack, features, architecture, expected_output, skills, resume_description, interview_questions) VALUES
('Software Development Engineer', 'Command-line To-Do with Priorities', 'beginner', 'Practise clean code and data structures.', 'Command-line To-Do with Priorities is a beginner project for aspiring Software Development Engineers. Practise clean code and data structures. The goal is to build a working solution with priority queue of tasks and persistence, then extend it with search and unit tests.', '["Java/Python","Heap","File I/O"]'::jsonb, '["Priority queue of tasks","Persistence","Search","Unit tests"]'::jsonb, 'Modular design with clear interfaces, efficient data structures, automated tests and a simple CLI/API front end. For this project: Java/Python, Heap, File I/O.', 'A working command-line to-do with priorities with: Priority queue of tasks; Persistence; Search; Unit tests. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Java/Python","Heap","File I/O","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a command-line to-do with priorities using Java/Python, Heap, File I/O that supports priority queue of tasks, persistence, search; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Command-line To-Do with Priorities.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Persistence\"?","Which data structures did you use and why?","What is the time complexity of your core operations?","How did you test edge cases?","How would you extend Command-line To-Do with Priorities if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Software Development Engineer', 'Sudoku Solver', 'beginner', 'Apply backtracking to a real puzzle.', 'Sudoku Solver is a beginner project for aspiring Software Development Engineers. Apply backtracking to a real puzzle. The goal is to build a working solution with backtracking solver and input validation, then extend it with step-by-step mode and timing.', '["Python/Java","Backtracking"]'::jsonb, '["Backtracking solver","Input validation","Step-by-step mode","Timing"]'::jsonb, 'Modular design with clear interfaces, efficient data structures, automated tests and a simple CLI/API front end. For this project: Python/Java, Backtracking.', 'A working sudoku solver with: Backtracking solver; Input validation; Step-by-step mode; Timing. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python/Java","Backtracking","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a sudoku solver using Python/Java, Backtracking that supports backtracking solver, input validation, step-by-step mode; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Sudoku Solver.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Input validation\"?","Which data structures did you use and why?","What is the time complexity of your core operations?","How did you test edge cases?","How would you extend Sudoku Solver if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
