('Data Scientist', 'Student Performance Predictor', 'beginner', 'Identify students who need support.', 'Student Performance Predictor is a beginner project for aspiring Data Scientists. Identify students who need support. The goal is to build a working solution with feature analysis and classification, then extend it with fairness check and report.', '["Python","pandas","scikit-learn"]'::jsonb, '["Feature analysis","Classification","Fairness check","Report"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, pandas, scikit-learn.', 'A working student performance predictor with: Feature analysis; Classification; Fairness check; Report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","pandas","scikit-learn","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a student performance predictor using Python, pandas, scikit-learn that supports feature analysis, classification, fairness check; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Student Performance Predictor.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Classification\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Student Performance Predictor if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Spam Detector', 'beginner', 'Filter unwanted messages.', 'Spam Detector is a beginner project for aspiring Data Scientists. Filter unwanted messages. The goal is to build a working solution with text cleaning and tf-idf, then extend it with naive bayes and precision/recall.', '["Python","scikit-learn"]'::jsonb, '["Text cleaning","TF-IDF","Naive Bayes","Precision/recall"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, scikit-learn.', 'A working spam detector with: Text cleaning; TF-IDF; Naive Bayes; Precision/recall. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","scikit-learn","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a spam detector using Python, scikit-learn that supports text cleaning, tf-idf, naive bayes; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Spam Detector.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"TF-IDF\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Spam Detector if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Exploratory Analysis Notebook', 'beginner', 'Show strong EDA skills on an open dataset.', 'Exploratory Analysis Notebook is a beginner project for aspiring Data Scientists. Show strong EDA skills on an open dataset. The goal is to build a working solution with data quality checks and univariate/bivariate plots, then extend it with hypotheses and conclusions.', '["Python","Jupyter","seaborn"]'::jsonb, '["Data quality checks","Univariate/bivariate plots","Hypotheses","Conclusions"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, Jupyter, seaborn.', 'A working exploratory analysis notebook with: Data quality checks; Univariate/bivariate plots; Hypotheses; Conclusions. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","Jupyter","seaborn","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a exploratory analysis notebook using Python, Jupyter, seaborn that supports data quality checks, univariate/bivariate plots, hypotheses; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Exploratory Analysis Notebook.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Univariate/bivariate plots\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Exploratory Analysis Notebook if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Customer Churn Prediction', 'intermediate', 'Predict which customers will leave.', 'Customer Churn Prediction is a intermediate project for aspiring Data Scientists. Predict which customers will leave. The goal is to build a working solution with imbalanced data handling and gradient boosting, then extend it with shap explanations and business metrics.', '["Python","XGBoost","SHAP"]'::jsonb, '["Imbalanced data handling","Gradient boosting","SHAP explanations","Business metrics"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, XGBoost, SHAP.', 'A working customer churn prediction with: Imbalanced data handling; Gradient boosting; SHAP explanations; Business metrics. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","XGBoost","SHAP","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a customer churn prediction using Python, XGBoost, SHAP that supports imbalanced data handling, gradient boosting, shap explanations; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Customer Churn Prediction.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Gradient boosting\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Customer Churn Prediction if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Sentiment Analysis of Reviews', 'intermediate', 'Understand customer opinion at scale.', 'Sentiment Analysis of Reviews is a intermediate project for aspiring Data Scientists. Understand customer opinion at scale. The goal is to build a working solution with text preprocessing and classical vs transformer models, then extend it with evaluation and dashboard.', '["Python","scikit-learn","Hugging Face"]'::jsonb, '["Text preprocessing","Classical vs transformer models","Evaluation","Dashboard"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, scikit-learn, Hugging Face.', 'A working sentiment analysis of reviews with: Text preprocessing; Classical vs transformer models; Evaluation; Dashboard. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","scikit-learn","Hugging Face","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a sentiment analysis of reviews using Python, scikit-learn, Hugging Face that supports text preprocessing, classical vs transformer models, evaluation; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Sentiment Analysis of Reviews.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Classical vs transformer models\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Sentiment Analysis of Reviews if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Credit Risk Scoring', 'intermediate', 'Estimate default risk responsibly.', 'Credit Risk Scoring is a intermediate project for aspiring Data Scientists. Estimate default risk responsibly. The goal is to build a working solution with feature engineering and logistic regression baseline, then extend it with roc-auc and fairness analysis.', '["Python","scikit-learn"]'::jsonb, '["Feature engineering","Logistic regression baseline","ROC-AUC","Fairness analysis"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, scikit-learn.', 'A working credit risk scoring with: Feature engineering; Logistic regression baseline; ROC-AUC; Fairness analysis. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","scikit-learn","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a credit risk scoring using Python, scikit-learn that supports feature engineering, logistic regression baseline, roc-auc; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Credit Risk Scoring.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Logistic regression baseline\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Credit Risk Scoring if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Recommendation System', 'intermediate', 'Suggest items users may like.', 'Recommendation System is a intermediate project for aspiring Data Scientists. Suggest items users may like. The goal is to build a working solution with collaborative filtering and content features, then extend it with offline metrics and simple api.', '["Python","Surprise/implicit","FastAPI"]'::jsonb, '["Collaborative filtering","Content features","Offline metrics","Simple API"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, Surprise/implicit, FastAPI.', 'A working recommendation system with: Collaborative filtering; Content features; Offline metrics; Simple API. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","Surprise/implicit","FastAPI","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a recommendation system using Python, Surprise/implicit, FastAPI that supports collaborative filtering, content features, offline metrics; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Recommendation System.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Content features\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Recommendation System if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Time-series Sales Forecasting', 'intermediate', 'Forecast weekly demand.', 'Time-series Sales Forecasting is a intermediate project for aspiring Data Scientists. Forecast weekly demand. The goal is to build a working solution with seasonality analysis and arima/prophet/gbm, then extend it with backtesting and visual report.', '["Python","statsmodels"]'::jsonb, '["Seasonality analysis","ARIMA/Prophet/GBM","Backtesting","Visual report"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, statsmodels.', 'A working time-series sales forecasting with: Seasonality analysis; ARIMA/Prophet/GBM; Backtesting; Visual report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","statsmodels","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a time-series sales forecasting using Python, statsmodels that supports seasonality analysis, arima/prophet/gbm, backtesting; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Time-series Sales Forecasting.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"ARIMA/Prophet/GBM\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Time-series Sales Forecasting if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Model Deployment with Monitoring', 'advanced', 'Models must work after deployment.', 'Model Deployment with Monitoring is a advanced project for aspiring Data Scientists. Models must work after deployment. The goal is to build a working solution with model api and input validation, then extend it with drift monitoring and retraining pipeline.', '["Python","FastAPI","Docker","MLflow"]'::jsonb, '["Model API","Input validation","Drift monitoring","Retraining pipeline"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, FastAPI, Docker, MLflow.', 'A working model deployment with monitoring with: Model API; Input validation; Drift monitoring; Retraining pipeline. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","FastAPI","Docker","MLflow","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a model deployment with monitoring using Python, FastAPI, Docker that supports model api, input validation, drift monitoring; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Model Deployment with Monitoring.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Input validation\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Model Deployment with Monitoring if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Fraud Detection System', 'advanced', 'Catch fraudulent transactions with few false alarms.', 'Fraud Detection System is a advanced project for aspiring Data Scientists. Catch fraudulent transactions with few false alarms. The goal is to build a working solution with extreme imbalance and anomaly + supervised models, then extend it with threshold tuning and cost analysis.', '["Python","LightGBM","imbalanced-learn"]'::jsonb, '["Extreme imbalance","Anomaly + supervised models","Threshold tuning","Cost analysis"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, LightGBM, imbalanced-learn.', 'A working fraud detection system with: Extreme imbalance; Anomaly + supervised models; Threshold tuning; Cost analysis. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","LightGBM","imbalanced-learn","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a fraud detection system using Python, LightGBM, imbalanced-learn that supports extreme imbalance, anomaly + supervised models, threshold tuning; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Fraud Detection System.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Anomaly + supervised models\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Fraud Detection System if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Causal Impact Analysis', 'advanced', 'Did a marketing campaign actually work?', 'Causal Impact Analysis is a advanced project for aspiring Data Scientists. Did a marketing campaign actually work? The goal is to build a working solution with causal framing and difference-in-differences, then extend it with synthetic control and report.', '["Python","statsmodels"]'::jsonb, '["Causal framing","Difference-in-differences","Synthetic control","Report"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, statsmodels.', 'A working causal impact analysis with: Causal framing; Difference-in-differences; Synthetic control; Report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","statsmodels","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a causal impact analysis using Python, statsmodels that supports causal framing, difference-in-differences, synthetic control; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Causal Impact Analysis.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Difference-in-differences\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Causal Impact Analysis if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Image Classification with Transfer Learning', 'advanced', 'Classify images with limited data.', 'Image Classification with Transfer Learning is a advanced project for aspiring Data Scientists. Classify images with limited data. The goal is to build a working solution with pretrained cnn and augmentation, then extend it with evaluation and grad-cam explanations.', '["Python","PyTorch/TensorFlow"]'::jsonb, '["Pretrained CNN","Augmentation","Evaluation","Grad-CAM explanations"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, PyTorch/TensorFlow.', 'A working image classification with transfer learning with: Pretrained CNN; Augmentation; Evaluation; Grad-CAM explanations. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","PyTorch/TensorFlow","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a image classification with transfer learning using Python, PyTorch/TensorFlow that supports pretrained cnn, augmentation, evaluation; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Image Classification with Transfer Learning.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Augmentation\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Image Classification with Transfer Learning if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Data Scientist', 'Experimentation Platform Prototype', 'advanced', 'Teams need repeatable A/B testing.', 'Experimentation Platform Prototype is a advanced project for aspiring Data Scientists. Teams need repeatable A/B testing. The goal is to build a working solution with randomisation service and metric computation, then extend it with sequential testing and dashboard.', '["Python","SQL","Streamlit"]'::jsonb, '["Randomisation service","Metric computation","Sequential testing","Dashboard"]'::jsonb, 'ML workflow: problem framing → data collection → EDA → feature engineering → model training/validation → evaluation → deployment API → monitoring. For this project: Python, SQL, Streamlit.', 'A working experimentation platform prototype with: Randomisation service; Metric computation; Sequential testing; Dashboard. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","SQL","Streamlit","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a experimentation platform prototype using Python, SQL, Streamlit that supports randomisation service, metric computation, sequential testing; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Experimentation Platform Prototype.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Metric computation\"?","How did you validate your model?","How did you avoid data leakage?","How would you explain the model to a business user?","How would you extend Experimentation Platform Prototype if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb);
