('AI/ML Engineer', 'Handwritten Digit Recogniser', 'beginner', 'Learn neural network basics.', 'Handwritten Digit Recogniser is a beginner project for aspiring AI/ML Engineers. Learn neural network basics. The goal is to build a working solution with mlp and cnn models and training curves, then extend it with web demo canvas and accuracy report.', '["Python","PyTorch/TensorFlow"]'::jsonb, '["MLP and CNN models","Training curves","Web demo canvas","Accuracy report"]'::jsonb, 'ML system: data pipeline → training code with experiment tracking → model registry → inference service (REST) → monitoring and feedback loop. For this project: Python, PyTorch/TensorFlow.', 'A working handwritten digit recogniser with: MLP and CNN models; Training curves; Web demo canvas; Accuracy report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","PyTorch/TensorFlow","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a handwritten digit recogniser using Python, PyTorch/TensorFlow that supports mlp and cnn models, training curves, web demo canvas; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Handwritten Digit Recogniser.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Training curves\"?","How did you choose the model architecture?","How do you serve the model in production?","How do you detect model drift?","How would you extend Handwritten Digit Recogniser if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('AI/ML Engineer', 'Linear Regression from Scratch', 'beginner', 'Understand gradient descent deeply.', 'Linear Regression from Scratch is a beginner project for aspiring AI/ML Engineers. Understand gradient descent deeply. The goal is to build a working solution with numpy implementation and learning-rate experiments, then extend it with compare with scikit-learn and plots.', '["Python","NumPy"]'::jsonb, '["NumPy implementation","Learning-rate experiments","Compare with scikit-learn","Plots"]'::jsonb, 'ML system: data pipeline → training code with experiment tracking → model registry → inference service (REST) → monitoring and feedback loop. For this project: Python, NumPy.', 'A working linear regression from scratch with: NumPy implementation; Learning-rate experiments; Compare with scikit-learn; Plots. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","NumPy","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a linear regression from scratch using Python, NumPy that supports numpy implementation, learning-rate experiments, compare with scikit-learn; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Linear Regression from Scratch.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Learning-rate experiments\"?","How did you choose the model architecture?","How do you serve the model in production?","How do you detect model drift?","How would you extend Linear Regression from Scratch if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('AI/ML Engineer', 'Face Mask / Object Detector Demo', 'beginner', 'Apply a pretrained detector to images.', 'Face Mask / Object Detector Demo is a beginner project for aspiring AI/ML Engineers. Apply a pretrained detector to images. The goal is to build a working solution with pretrained model inference and webcam demo, then extend it with confidence thresholds and limitations write-up.', '["Python","OpenCV"]'::jsonb, '["Pretrained model inference","Webcam demo","Confidence thresholds","Limitations write-up"]'::jsonb, 'ML system: data pipeline → training code with experiment tracking → model registry → inference service (REST) → monitoring and feedback loop. For this project: Python, OpenCV.', 'A working face mask / object detector demo with: Pretrained model inference; Webcam demo; Confidence thresholds; Limitations write-up. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","OpenCV","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a face mask / object detector demo using Python, OpenCV that supports pretrained model inference, webcam demo, confidence thresholds; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Face Mask / Object Detector Demo.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Webcam demo\"?","How did you choose the model architecture?","How do you serve the model in production?","How do you detect model drift?","How would you extend Face Mask / Object Detector Demo if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('AI/ML Engineer', 'Text Summariser', 'beginner', 'Summarise long articles.', 'Text Summariser is a beginner project for aspiring AI/ML Engineers. Summarise long articles. The goal is to build a working solution with extractive summarisation and pretrained abstractive model, then extend it with compare outputs and simple ui.', '["Python","Hugging Face"]'::jsonb, '["Extractive summarisation","Pretrained abstractive model","Compare outputs","Simple UI"]'::jsonb, 'ML system: data pipeline → training code with experiment tracking → model registry → inference service (REST) → monitoring and feedback loop. For this project: Python, Hugging Face.', 'A working text summariser with: Extractive summarisation; Pretrained abstractive model; Compare outputs; Simple UI. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","Hugging Face","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a text summariser using Python, Hugging Face that supports extractive summarisation, pretrained abstractive model, compare outputs; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Text Summariser.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Pretrained abstractive model\"?","How did you choose the model architecture?","How do you serve the model in production?","How do you detect model drift?","How would you extend Text Summariser if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('AI/ML Engineer', 'Movie Genre Classifier', 'beginner', 'Classify plots into genres.', 'Movie Genre Classifier is a beginner project for aspiring AI/ML Engineers. Classify plots into genres. The goal is to build a working solution with text features and multi-label classification, then extend it with evaluation and error analysis.', '["Python","scikit-learn"]'::jsonb, '["Text features","Multi-label classification","Evaluation","Error analysis"]'::jsonb, 'ML system: data pipeline → training code with experiment tracking → model registry → inference service (REST) → monitoring and feedback loop. For this project: Python, scikit-learn.', 'A working movie genre classifier with: Text features; Multi-label classification; Evaluation; Error analysis. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","scikit-learn","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a movie genre classifier using Python, scikit-learn that supports text features, multi-label classification, evaluation; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Movie Genre Classifier.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Multi-label classification\"?","How did you choose the model architecture?","How do you serve the model in production?","How do you detect model drift?","How would you extend Movie Genre Classifier if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('AI/ML Engineer', 'Chatbot with Retrieval (RAG)', 'intermediate', 'Answer questions from your college documents.', 'Chatbot with Retrieval (RAG) is a intermediate project for aspiring AI/ML Engineers. Answer questions from your college documents. The goal is to build a working solution with document chunking and embeddings + vector search, then extend it with llm answer with citations and evaluation set.', '["Python","Vector DB","LLM API"]'::jsonb, '["Document chunking","Embeddings + vector search","LLM answer with citations","Evaluation set"]'::jsonb, 'ML system: data pipeline → training code with experiment tracking → model registry → inference service (REST) → monitoring and feedback loop. For this project: Python, Vector DB, LLM API.', 'A working chatbot with retrieval (rag) with: Document chunking; Embeddings + vector search; LLM answer with citations; Evaluation set. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","Vector DB","LLM API","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a chatbot with retrieval (rag) using Python, Vector DB, LLM API that supports document chunking, embeddings + vector search, llm answer with citations; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Chatbot with Retrieval (RAG).","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Embeddings + vector search\"?","How did you choose the model architecture?","How do you serve the model in production?","How do you detect model drift?","How would you extend Chatbot with Retrieval (RAG) if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
