('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Phishing Awareness Quiz', 'beginner', 'People fall for phishing emails.', 'Phishing Awareness Quiz is a beginner project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. People fall for phishing emails. The goal is to build a working solution with realistic (fictional) examples and explanations, then extend it with score tracking and tips.', '["HTML","JavaScript"]'::jsonb, '["Realistic (fictional) examples","Explanations","Score tracking","Tips"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: HTML, JavaScript.', 'A working phishing awareness quiz with: Realistic (fictional) examples; Explanations; Score tracking; Tips. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["HTML","JavaScript","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a phishing awareness quiz using HTML, JavaScript that supports realistic (fictional) examples, explanations, score tracking; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Phishing Awareness Quiz.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Explanations\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Phishing Awareness Quiz if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'File Integrity Monitor', 'beginner', 'Detect unauthorised file changes.', 'File Integrity Monitor is a beginner project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Detect unauthorised file changes. The goal is to build a working solution with hash baseline and periodic checks, then extend it with alerts and report.', '["Python","hashlib"]'::jsonb, '["Hash baseline","Periodic checks","Alerts","Report"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Python, hashlib.', 'A working file integrity monitor with: Hash baseline; Periodic checks; Alerts; Report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","hashlib","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a file integrity monitor using Python, hashlib that supports hash baseline, periodic checks, alerts; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your File Integrity Monitor.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Periodic checks\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend File Integrity Monitor if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Log Analyser for Failed Logins', 'beginner', 'Brute-force attempts hide in logs.', 'Log Analyser for Failed Logins is a beginner project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Brute-force attempts hide in logs. The goal is to build a working solution with parse auth logs and detect bursts, then extend it with geoip summary and alerts.', '["Python","Regex"]'::jsonb, '["Parse auth logs","Detect bursts","GeoIP summary","Alerts"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Python, Regex.', 'A working log analyser for failed logins with: Parse auth logs; Detect bursts; GeoIP summary; Alerts. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","Regex","Fundamentals","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a log analyser for failed logins using Python, Regex that supports parse auth logs, detect bursts, geoip summary; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Log Analyser for Failed Logins.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Detect bursts\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Log Analyser for Failed Logins if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Vulnerable App Lab Write-ups', 'intermediate', 'Learn web vulnerabilities legally.', 'Vulnerable App Lab Write-ups is a intermediate project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Learn web vulnerabilities legally. The goal is to build a working solution with set up an intentionally vulnerable lab app locally and exploit and document owasp top 10 issues, then extend it with fixes and write-ups.', '["OWASP Juice Shop/DVWA","Burp Suite"]'::jsonb, '["Set up an intentionally vulnerable lab app locally","Exploit and document OWASP Top 10 issues","Fixes","Write-ups"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: OWASP Juice Shop/DVWA, Burp Suite.', 'A working vulnerable app lab write-ups with: Set up an intentionally vulnerable lab app locally; Exploit and document OWASP Top 10 issues; Fixes; Write-ups. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["OWASP Juice Shop/DVWA","Burp Suite","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a vulnerable app lab write-ups using OWASP Juice Shop/DVWA, Burp Suite that supports set up an intentionally vulnerable lab app locally, exploit and document owasp top 10 issues, fixes; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Vulnerable App Lab Write-ups.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Exploit and document OWASP Top 10 issues\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Vulnerable App Lab Write-ups if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'SIEM Home Lab', 'intermediate', 'Practise detection engineering.', 'SIEM Home Lab is a intermediate project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Practise detection engineering. The goal is to build a working solution with collect logs from vms and detection rules, then extend it with dashboards and simulated attacks in the lab.', '["Elastic/Wazuh","VirtualBox"]'::jsonb, '["Collect logs from VMs","Detection rules","Dashboards","Simulated attacks in the lab"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Elastic/Wazuh, VirtualBox.', 'A working siem home lab with: Collect logs from VMs; Detection rules; Dashboards; Simulated attacks in the lab. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Elastic/Wazuh","VirtualBox","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a siem home lab using Elastic/Wazuh, VirtualBox that supports collect logs from vms, detection rules, dashboards; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your SIEM Home Lab.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Detection rules\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend SIEM Home Lab if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Secure Login Implementation', 'intermediate', 'Many apps implement auth unsafely.', 'Secure Login Implementation is a intermediate project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Many apps implement auth unsafely. The goal is to build a working solution with bcrypt/argon2 and rate limiting, then extend it with mfa (totp) and security tests.', '["Node.js/Python","TOTP"]'::jsonb, '["bcrypt/argon2","Rate limiting","MFA (TOTP)","Security tests"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Node.js/Python, TOTP.', 'A working secure login implementation with: bcrypt/argon2; Rate limiting; MFA (TOTP); Security tests. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Node.js/Python","TOTP","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a secure login implementation using Node.js/Python, TOTP that supports bcrypt/argon2, rate limiting, mfa (totp); documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Secure Login Implementation.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Rate limiting\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Secure Login Implementation if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Network Traffic Analyser', 'intermediate', 'Spot suspicious traffic patterns.', 'Network Traffic Analyser is a intermediate project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Spot suspicious traffic patterns. The goal is to build a working solution with packet capture analysis and protocol stats, then extend it with anomaly flags and report.', '["Wireshark","Python","Scapy"]'::jsonb, '["Packet capture analysis","Protocol stats","Anomaly flags","Report"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Wireshark, Python, Scapy.', 'A working network traffic analyser with: Packet capture analysis; Protocol stats; Anomaly flags; Report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Wireshark","Python","Scapy","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a network traffic analyser using Wireshark, Python, Scapy that supports packet capture analysis, protocol stats, anomaly flags; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Network Traffic Analyser.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Protocol stats\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Network Traffic Analyser if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Incident Response Playbooks', 'intermediate', 'Teams panic without a plan.', 'Incident Response Playbooks is a intermediate project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Teams panic without a plan. The goal is to build a working solution with playbooks for common incidents and roles and timelines, then extend it with tabletop exercise and lessons learned template.', '["Markdown","Process design"]'::jsonb, '["Playbooks for common incidents","Roles and timelines","Tabletop exercise","Lessons learned template"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Markdown, Process design.', 'A working incident response playbooks with: Playbooks for common incidents; Roles and timelines; Tabletop exercise; Lessons learned template. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Markdown","Process design","System integration","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a incident response playbooks using Markdown, Process design that supports playbooks for common incidents, roles and timelines, tabletop exercise; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Incident Response Playbooks.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Roles and timelines\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Incident Response Playbooks if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Threat Intelligence Dashboard', 'advanced', 'Track relevant threats for an organisation.', 'Threat Intelligence Dashboard is a advanced project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Track relevant threats for an organisation. The goal is to build a working solution with ingest public threat feeds and indicator matching, then extend it with dashboards and weekly brief.', '["Python","Elastic","STIX/TAXII"]'::jsonb, '["Ingest public threat feeds","Indicator matching","Dashboards","Weekly brief"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Python, Elastic, STIX/TAXII.', 'A working threat intelligence dashboard with: Ingest public threat feeds; Indicator matching; Dashboards; Weekly brief. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","Elastic","STIX/TAXII","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a threat intelligence dashboard using Python, Elastic, STIX/TAXII that supports ingest public threat feeds, indicator matching, dashboards; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Threat Intelligence Dashboard.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Indicator matching\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Threat Intelligence Dashboard if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Cloud Security Posture Checker', 'advanced', 'Misconfigured cloud resources leak data.', 'Cloud Security Posture Checker is a advanced project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Misconfigured cloud resources leak data. The goal is to build a working solution with scan own account for public buckets/open ports and cis benchmark checks, then extend it with remediation guidance and report.', '["Python","Cloud SDKs"]'::jsonb, '["Scan own account for public buckets/open ports","CIS benchmark checks","Remediation guidance","Report"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Python, Cloud SDKs.', 'A working cloud security posture checker with: Scan own account for public buckets/open ports; CIS benchmark checks; Remediation guidance; Report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Python","Cloud SDKs","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a cloud security posture checker using Python, Cloud SDKs that supports scan own account for public buckets/open ports, cis benchmark checks, remediation guidance; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Cloud Security Posture Checker.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"CIS benchmark checks\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Cloud Security Posture Checker if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Malware Analysis Sandbox Lab', 'advanced', 'Understand malicious behaviour safely.', 'Malware Analysis Sandbox Lab is a advanced project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Understand malicious behaviour safely. The goal is to build a working solution with isolated vm lab and static analysis, then extend it with behaviour monitoring and ioc report.', '["VirtualBox","Sysinternals-style tools"]'::jsonb, '["Isolated VM lab","Static analysis","Behaviour monitoring","IOC report"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: VirtualBox, Sysinternals-style tools.', 'A working malware analysis sandbox lab with: Isolated VM lab; Static analysis; Behaviour monitoring; IOC report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["VirtualBox","Sysinternals-style tools","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a malware analysis sandbox lab using VirtualBox, Sysinternals-style tools that supports isolated vm lab, static analysis, behaviour monitoring; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Malware Analysis Sandbox Lab.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Static analysis\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Malware Analysis Sandbox Lab if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Zero-Trust Access Prototype', 'advanced', 'VPNs give too much implicit trust.', 'Zero-Trust Access Prototype is a advanced project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. VPNs give too much implicit trust. The goal is to build a working solution with identity-aware proxy and device posture checks, then extend it with per-request authorisation and audit logs.', '["Reverse proxy","OAuth/OIDC"]'::jsonb, '["Identity-aware proxy","Device posture checks","Per-request authorisation","Audit logs"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Reverse proxy, OAuth/OIDC.', 'A working zero-trust access prototype with: Identity-aware proxy; Device posture checks; Per-request authorisation; Audit logs. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Reverse proxy","OAuth/OIDC","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a zero-trust access prototype using Reverse proxy, OAuth/OIDC that supports identity-aware proxy, device posture checks, per-request authorisation; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Zero-Trust Access Prototype.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Device posture checks\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Zero-Trust Access Prototype if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb),
('Cybersecurity Analyst', 'Secure Code Review Toolkit', 'advanced', 'Catch vulnerabilities before release.', 'Secure Code Review Toolkit is a advanced project for aspiring Cybersecurity Analysts. Catch vulnerabilities before release. The goal is to build a working solution with static analysis rules and dependency scanning, then extend it with ci integration and developer report.', '["Semgrep-style rules","GitHub Actions"]'::jsonb, '["Static analysis rules","Dependency scanning","CI integration","Developer report"]'::jsonb, 'Security workflow: asset inventory → threat modelling → controls (prevent/detect) → logging to a SIEM → alert triage → incident response and reporting. For this project: Semgrep-style rules, GitHub Actions.', 'A working secure code review toolkit with: Static analysis rules; Dependency scanning; CI integration; Developer report. Include a README with screenshots, setup steps and (where possible) a live demo link.', '["Semgrep-style rules","GitHub Actions","Scalable design","Problem solving","Documentation"]'::jsonb, 'Built a secure code review toolkit using Semgrep-style rules, GitHub Actions that supports static analysis rules, dependency scanning, ci integration; documented setup and design decisions on GitHub.', '["Explain the architecture of your Secure Code Review Toolkit.","What was the hardest part of implementing \"Dependency scanning\"?","How did you identify the vulnerabilities?","How would you prioritise findings?","How do you stay within legal and ethical boundaries when testing?","How would you extend Secure Code Review Toolkit if it had 10x more users?"]'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO companies (slug, name, type, overview, products, careers_url, headquarters) VALUES
('google', 'Google', 'product', 'Google, a subsidiary of Alphabet, builds internet search, advertising, cloud computing, Android and AI products used by billions of people.', 'Google Search, Android, Chrome, YouTube, Google Cloud, Workspace (Gmail, Docs), Maps, Pixel devices', 'https://careers.google.com/', 'Mountain View, California, USA'),
('amazon', 'Amazon', 'product', 'Amazon operates e-commerce marketplaces and Amazon Web Services (AWS), the largest cloud provider, plus devices and streaming.', 'Amazon.com / Amazon.in marketplace, AWS, Prime Video, Alexa, Kindle', 'https://www.amazon.jobs/', 'Seattle, Washington, USA'),
('microsoft', 'Microsoft', 'product', 'Microsoft builds operating systems, productivity software, developer tools, gaming and the Azure cloud platform.', 'Windows, Microsoft 365, Azure, GitHub, Visual Studio / VS Code, LinkedIn, Xbox', 'https://careers.microsoft.com/', 'Redmond, Washington, USA'),
('meta', 'Meta', 'product', 'Meta Platforms builds social and communication products and invests in AI and virtual/augmented reality.', 'Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp, Messenger, Threads, Meta Quest', 'https://www.metacareers.com/', 'Menlo Park, California, USA'),
('apple', 'Apple', 'product', 'Apple designs consumer hardware, operating systems, software and services with tight hardware-software integration.', 'iPhone, Mac, iPad, Apple Watch, iOS, macOS, App Store, iCloud', 'https://www.apple.com/careers/', 'Cupertino, California, USA'),
('adobe', 'Adobe', 'product', 'Adobe creates software for creativity, documents and digital marketing.', 'Photoshop, Illustrator, Acrobat/PDF, Premiere Pro, Adobe Express, Experience Cloud', 'https://www.adobe.com/careers.html', 'San Jose, California, USA'),
('nvidia', 'NVIDIA', 'product', 'NVIDIA designs GPUs and accelerated computing platforms used for graphics, AI, data centres and autonomous systems.', 'GeForce GPUs, data-centre GPUs, CUDA, AI software platforms, DRIVE', 'https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/about-nvidia/careers/', 'Santa Clara, California, USA'),
('oracle', 'Oracle', 'product', 'Oracle provides database software, enterprise applications and cloud infrastructure.', 'Oracle Database, Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI), Java SE stewardship, enterprise applications (ERP, HCM)', 'https://www.oracle.com/careers/', 'Austin, Texas, USA'),
('salesforce', 'Salesforce', 'product', 'Salesforce is a leading customer relationship management (CRM) software company delivering cloud applications.', 'Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, Slack, Tableau, MuleSoft, Platform/Agentforce', 'https://careers.salesforce.com/', 'San Francisco, California, USA'),
('uber', 'Uber', 'product', 'Uber runs a technology platform for ride-hailing, food delivery and freight.', 'Uber rides, Uber Eats, Uber Freight', 'https://www.uber.com/us/en/careers/', 'San Francisco, California, USA'),
('flipkart', 'Flipkart', 'product', 'Flipkart is one of India''s largest e-commerce marketplaces, part of the Walmart group.', 'Flipkart marketplace, Flipkart Minutes/quick commerce, Myntra (group), Cleartrip (group)', 'https://www.flipkartcareers.com/', 'Bengaluru, India'),
('phonepe', 'PhonePe', 'product', 'PhonePe is an Indian digital payments and financial services company built around UPI.', 'PhonePe UPI app, payment gateway, insurance and investments distribution, Indus Appstore', 'https://www.phonepe.com/careers/', 'Bengaluru, India'),
('razorpay', 'Razorpay', 'product', 'Razorpay provides online payment processing and banking solutions for businesses in India.', 'Payment gateway, RazorpayX business banking, payroll, payment links', 'https://razorpay.com/jobs/', 'Bengaluru, India'),
('qualcomm', 'Qualcomm', 'product', 'Qualcomm designs wireless technology and semiconductors, including mobile processors and modems.', 'Snapdragon platforms, modems, wireless and automotive chips', 'https://careers.qualcomm.com/', 'San Diego, California, USA'),
('intel', 'Intel', 'product', 'Intel designs and manufactures processors and semiconductor technology.', 'Core and Xeon processors, foundry services, networking and AI accelerators', 'https://jobs.intel.com/', 'Santa Clara, California, USA'),
('zoho', 'Zoho', 'product', 'Zoho Corporation builds a large suite of business software products, developed largely in-house.', 'Zoho CRM, Zoho Mail, Zoho Books, Zoho Creator, Zoho Workplace, ManageEngine', 'https://www.zoho.com/careers.html', 'Chennai, India'),
('freshworks', 'Freshworks', 'product', 'Freshworks builds business software for customer service, IT service management and sales.', 'Freshdesk, Freshservice, Freshsales, Freshchat', 'https://careers.freshworks.com/', 'San Mateo, California, USA (founded in Chennai, India)'),
('tcs', 'TCS (Tata Consultancy Services)', 'service', 'TCS is a global IT services, consulting and business solutions company and part of the Tata Group.', 'IT services, consulting, cloud and digital transformation, TCS BaNCS and other platforms', 'https://www.tcs.com/careers', 'Mumbai, India'),
('infosys', 'Infosys', 'service', 'Infosys provides IT services, consulting and digital transformation for clients worldwide.', 'IT services and consulting, Finacle banking platform, Infosys Topaz / Cobalt offerings', 'https://www.infosys.com/careers.html', 'Bengaluru, India'),
('wipro', 'Wipro', 'service', 'Wipro is a global technology services and consulting company.', 'IT services, consulting, cloud, cybersecurity and engineering services', 'https://careers.wipro.com/', 'Bengaluru, India'),
('accenture', 'Accenture', 'service', 'Accenture is a global professional services company offering consulting, technology and operations services.', 'Consulting, technology services, cloud, security, operations', 'https://www.accenture.com/in-en/careers', 'Dublin, Ireland'),
('cognizant', 'Cognizant', 'service', 'Cognizant provides IT services, consulting and digital engineering.', 'IT services, digital engineering, consulting, business process services', 'https://careers.cognizant.com/', 'Teaneck, New Jersey, USA'),
('capgemini', 'Capgemini', 'service', 'Capgemini is a global consulting, technology services and digital transformation company.', 'Consulting, cloud, data and AI services, engineering (Capgemini Engineering)', 'https://www.capgemini.com/careers/', 'Paris, France'),
('hcltech', 'HCLTech', 'service', 'HCLTech is a global technology company providing IT services, engineering and software products.', 'IT and business services, engineering and R&D services, HCLSoftware products', 'https://www.hcltech.com/careers', 'Noida, India'),
('tech-mahindra', 'Tech Mahindra', 'service', 'Tech Mahindra, part of the Mahindra Group, provides digital transformation, consulting and IT services, with strength in telecom.', 'IT services, network services, consulting, engineering', 'https://careers.techmahindra.com/', 'Pune, India'),
('deloitte', 'Deloitte', 'service', 'Deloitte is a global professional services network providing audit, consulting, tax, risk and advisory services.', 'Consulting, technology implementation, audit and assurance, risk advisory', 'https://www.deloitte.com/global/en/careers.html', 'London, United Kingdom'),
('ibm', 'IBM', 'service', 'IBM provides hybrid cloud, AI and consulting services, and enterprise hardware and software.', 'IBM Cloud, watsonx AI, Red Hat (subsidiary), IBM Consulting, mainframes', 'https://www.ibm.com/careers', 'Armonk, New York, USA');
INSERT INTO company_preparation (company_id, section, title, content, verification, sort_order) VALUES
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'roles', 'Typical fresher roles', '["Software Engineer / SDE-1","Software Engineering Intern (for pre-final years)","Data / ML Engineer (team-dependent)","Quality / Test Engineer (some teams)"]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 0),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'eligibility', 'Eligibility (not verified)', '["BrainBridge has NOT verified current eligibility criteria for Google.","Criteria such as CGPA/percentage cut-offs, active backlogs, education gaps and eligible branches can change for every drive.","Always check the official careers page (https://careers.google.com/) and your college placement cell for the current notification."]'::jsonb, 'not_verified', 1),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'stages', 'Recruitment stages (general guidance)', '["Online assessment: 2-3 coding problems (sometimes with MCQs on CS fundamentals).","2-4 technical interviews: DSA problem solving, code quality, complexity, CS fundamentals and projects.","Some roles: design / low-level design or machine-coding round.","Behavioural / hiring-manager round on teamwork, ownership and motivation.","Interviews are known to emphasise problem solving and \"Googleyness\" (collaboration, humility, comfort with ambiguity)."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 2),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'technical', 'Technical topics to focus on', '["Strong DSA (graphs, DP, trees)","Clean, correct code under time pressure","Clear explanation of complexity and trade-offs","Operating systems, DBMS and networks fundamentals","Project architecture and trade-offs"]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 3),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'coding', 'Coding preparation', '["Solve the BrainBridge coding bank Medium and Hard problems (graphs, DP, heaps, sliding window).","Practise explaining your approach aloud before coding.","Always state time and space complexity and test edge cases.","Time yourself: ~25-30 minutes per medium problem."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 4),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'aptitude', 'Aptitude preparation', '["Aptitude is usually a smaller part for product companies; focus on probability, permutations and logical puzzles.","Use BrainBridge Quant → Probability and P&C quizzes."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 5),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'interview', 'Interview patterns (general guidance)', '["Clarify the problem → discuss brute force → optimise → code → test.","Interviewers value communication as much as the final code.","Be ready to go deep on one project you built.","Ask clarifying questions about constraints and edge cases."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 6),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'hr', 'Common HR questions to prepare', '["Tell me about yourself.","Why do you want to join Google?","What are your strengths and weaknesses?","Describe a challenge you faced in a team project.","Tell me about a time you took ownership beyond your assigned work.","Where do you see yourself in five years?"]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 7),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'roadmap', '4-week preparation roadmap', '["Week 1: Arrays, strings, hashing, two pointers, sliding window (BrainBridge DSA + Easy/Medium problems).","Week 2: Linked lists, stacks, queues, trees, BST, heaps.","Week 3: Graphs, DP, greedy, backtracking + 2 mock interviews (SDE track).","Week 4: CS fundamentals revision, project deep-dive, behavioural STAR stories, final mocks."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 8),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'resources', 'Recommended resources', '["Official careers site: https://careers.google.com/","BrainBridge: Learning Roadmap, Aptitude quizzes, Coding bank, Interview Preparation and Mock Interviews.","Your college placement cell and alumni from the company for current-year process details."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 9),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'google'), 'practice', 'Representative practice (original BrainBridge questions)', '["These are NOT previous-year questions — they are original BrainBridge practice items on the same topics.","Coding: try \"Pair with Target Sum\", \"Count the Islands\", \"Longest Rising Sequence\" and \"City Road Distances\" in the coding bank.","Aptitude: Probability and Permutations & Combinations quizzes (Hard).","Interview: take the matching mock interview track and review the rubric feedback."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 10),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'roles', 'Typical fresher roles', '["Software Engineer / SDE-1","Software Engineering Intern (for pre-final years)","Data / ML Engineer (team-dependent)","Quality / Test Engineer (some teams)"]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 0),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'eligibility', 'Eligibility (not verified)', '["BrainBridge has NOT verified current eligibility criteria for Amazon.","Criteria such as CGPA/percentage cut-offs, active backlogs, education gaps and eligible branches can change for every drive.","Always check the official careers page (https://www.amazon.jobs/) and your college placement cell for the current notification."]'::jsonb, 'not_verified', 1),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'stages', 'Recruitment stages (general guidance)', '["Online assessment: 2-3 coding problems (sometimes with MCQs on CS fundamentals).","2-4 technical interviews: DSA problem solving, code quality, complexity, CS fundamentals and projects.","Some roles: design / low-level design or machine-coding round.","Behavioural / hiring-manager round on teamwork, ownership and motivation.","Behavioural questions are commonly structured around Amazon''s published Leadership Principles — prepare STAR stories for them."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 2),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'technical', 'Technical topics to focus on', '["DSA with emphasis on arrays, trees, graphs, heaps","Object-oriented design","Behavioural answers mapped to Leadership Principles","Operating systems, DBMS and networks fundamentals","Project architecture and trade-offs"]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 3),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'coding', 'Coding preparation', '["Solve the BrainBridge coding bank Medium and Hard problems (graphs, DP, heaps, sliding window).","Practise explaining your approach aloud before coding.","Always state time and space complexity and test edge cases.","Time yourself: ~25-30 minutes per medium problem."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 4),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'aptitude', 'Aptitude preparation', '["Aptitude is usually a smaller part for product companies; focus on probability, permutations and logical puzzles.","Use BrainBridge Quant → Probability and P&C quizzes."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 5),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'interview', 'Interview patterns (general guidance)', '["Clarify the problem → discuss brute force → optimise → code → test.","Interviewers value communication as much as the final code.","Be ready to go deep on one project you built.","Ask clarifying questions about constraints and edge cases."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 6),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'hr', 'Common HR questions to prepare', '["Tell me about yourself.","Why do you want to join Amazon?","What are your strengths and weaknesses?","Describe a challenge you faced in a team project.","Tell me about a time you took ownership beyond your assigned work.","Where do you see yourself in five years?"]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 7),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'roadmap', '4-week preparation roadmap', '["Week 1: Arrays, strings, hashing, two pointers, sliding window (BrainBridge DSA + Easy/Medium problems).","Week 2: Linked lists, stacks, queues, trees, BST, heaps.","Week 3: Graphs, DP, greedy, backtracking + 2 mock interviews (SDE track).","Week 4: CS fundamentals revision, project deep-dive, behavioural STAR stories, final mocks."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 8),
((SELECT id FROM companies WHERE slug = 'amazon'), 'resources', 'Recommended resources', '["Official careers site: https://www.amazon.jobs/","BrainBridge: Learning Roadmap, Aptitude quizzes, Coding bank, Interview Preparation and Mock Interviews.","Your college placement cell and alumni from the company for current-year process details."]'::jsonb, 'guidance', 9),
